The `Aggregator` class can be initialized with initial aggregation parameters and an aggregation callback function, which processes the intermediate results for each batch of data points. The function accepts sensor data points and schedules their processing in a thread pool executor, ensuring low latency and high throughput. It also handles potential API failures gracefully by logging relevant information.

The `main()` function creates an instance of the Aggregator class, starts the main thread to process data points, and runs the aggregator itself in another thread. This allows for the aggregation of sensor data concurrently with other tasks, improving scalability and performance.

